                                "sense_id": "bb4adc7d-8427-37cb-8361-6d956443698e",
                                "text": "Leroy designed an instrument for grasping the stone using three or four claw-ended arms, an idea he found in the alphonsin of Alphonso Ferri, a Neapolitan surgeon of the 16th century, who used metal arms to seize and extract bullets from wounds."
